// REJECTS: Unexpected token 'Combined'. Valid alternatives: [';']
//
// `supportInfo:` carrying BOTH an Email block and a Combined block. The rule is
//     supportInfo: SUPPORT_INFO COLON (supportEmail | supportCombinedInfo) SEMI_COLON
// -- one alternative, then a semicolon. A parser generated from a looser reading (a repeated
// or optional group, which is how nearly every other field in this grammar is written) would
// accept the concatenation and silently keep whichever arm it saw last.
//
// The two arms are also not merely different spellings of the same record: they build
// different protocol classes (DataSpaceSupportEmail vs DataSpaceSupportCombinedInfo), so
// accepting both is not a harmless superset. See ../fixtures/t2-dataspace.pure and
// ../fixtures/t2-dataspace-email.pure -- the corpus needs TWO positive elements precisely
// because of this rule.
###DataSpace
DataSpace fixture::neg::BothSupportArms
{
  executionContexts:
  [
    {
      name: 'Context 1';
      mapping: fixture::neg::Mapping;
      defaultRuntime: fixture::neg::Runtime;
    }
  ];
  defaultExecutionContext: 'Context 1';
  supportInfo: Email {
    address: 'support@example.org';
  }
  Combined {
    website: 'https://example.org';
  };
}
